    "created_at": "2022-06-22T18:48:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-06-22T18:48:16Z",
    "body": "In WebKit `-webkit-background-size` and `background-size` are different longhands that share a computed value. It seems the only difference is in the parsing, so it should be easy to turn `-webkit-background-size` into a [legacy shorthand](https://www.w3.org/TR/css-cascade-5/#legacy-shorthand) of `background-size`, which would be the standard approach.\r\n\r\ngCS should round-trip, so either serialize `-webkit-background-size` and `background-size` differently, or always use 2 values.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
